.TH PODDOS 1 "2026-03-25" "poddos 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
poddos \- lightweight user-space container runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B poddos
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] pull \fI--url URL\fR
.br
.B poddos
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] start \fI[OPTIONS] [CMD...]R
.br
.B poddos
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] exec \fI[OPTIONS] CMD...R
.br
.B poddos
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] prune \fI[LAYER...]R
.SH DESCRIPTION
poddos is a small container runtime to pull Docker/OCI layers and run workloads in namespace-isolated containers.
.PP
Global options apply to all commands and include:
.TP
\fB-l, --layer PATH\fR
Layer storage path. Defaults to $LAYERPATH, $XDG_DATA_HOME/poddos, ~/.local/share/poddos, or /usr/local/share/poddos.
.TP
\fB-n, --name NAME\fR
Container name. Sets hostname/saved config and is used for PID/config files.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS pull
Pull a container image layer chain from a Docker registry URL.
.TP
\fB-u, --url URL\fR
URL for pull source (e.g., registry-1.docker.io/library/ubuntu:latest).
.PP
Example:
.nf
poddos --name ubuntu pull --url registry-1.docker.io/library/ubuntu:latest
.fi
.SS start
Create and start a container with a writable overlay and optional command.
.TP
\fB-o, --overlay PATH\fR
Overlay path (multiple uses allowed). Each new overlay layer is stacked, last one writable.
.TP
\fB-e, --env FOO=BAR\fR
Add environment variable to container process.
.TP
\fB-E, --ephemeral\fR
Ephemeral mode: top-level filesystem mounted tmpfs; changes discarded at container exit.
.TP
\fB--no-ephemeral\fR
Disable ephemeral mode explicitly.
.TP
\fB--net INTERFACE\fR
Enable network namespace with a macvlan interface inside container (macvlan0). Uses bridge mode, one container cannot be reached directly from host, containers can connect to each other. A wired host interface is required for macvlan to work reliably; wireless interfaces are typically unsupported or restricted.
.TP
\fB--mac MAC\fR
Set macvlan MAC address (for --net). If omitted, kernel random MAC is used.
.TP
\fB--dns DNS\fR
Set DNS server in container network namespace. If omitted, DHCP-provided DNS address is used.
.TP
\fB--net DHCP behavior\fR
When --net is provided and --dns is omitted, DNS/IP is obtained via DHCP by default.
.TP
\fB--bind FROM:TO\fR
Bind mount host path FROM into container path TO. TO defaults to FROM if omitted. Must use absolute paths.
.TP
\fB-C, --directory PATH\fR
Change into PATH inside container before executing command.
.PP
Network setup flow for --net:
- Enter network namespace.
- Create a macvlan device on host interface INTERFACE in bridge mode, name usually macvlan0 inside container.
- Container gets its IPv4 address via DHCP.
- Host cannot reach container directly because of macvlan isolation semantics.
.SS exec
Run a command inside an already running named container.
.TP
\fB-e, --env FOO=BAR\fR
Additional environment variable applied to command.
.PP
Example:
.nf
poddos --name ubuntu exec --env FOO=BAR /bin/bash -lc 'echo $FOO'
.fi
.SS prune
Clean up unused layer data.
.TP
\fB-a, --all\fR
Scan for unused layers and remove them.
.TP
\fB-f, --force\fR
Proceed without user confirmation in combination with --all.
.PP
Example:
.nf
poddos prune --all --force
poddos prune layer1 layer2
.fi
.SH USAGE EXAMPLES
.nf
# Pull the latest ubuntu image
poddos --name ubuntu pull --url registry-1.docker.io/library/ubuntu:latest

# Start container with overlay layers and a shell
poddos --name ubuntu start --overlay base --overlay user --env HOME=/root /bin/bash

# Start container with ephemeral overlay and networking
poddos --name netcontainer start --overlay base --net eth0 --mac 02:42:ac:11:00:02 --dns 8.8.8.8 /bin/sh

# Execute a command in running container
poddos --name ubuntu exec /bin/ls /

# Prune unused layers
poddos prune --all
.fi
.SH FILES
/usr/local/bin/poddos
/usr/local/share/man/man1/poddos.1.gz
.SH AUTHOR
Written by the poddos maintainer.
